# let hidden = { run: inside }; globalThis.shared = { run: outside }; made = new Function(text); made({ run: handed }); [1].map(mapper); hidden.run()
# The text of a function that `Function` makes runs in the global scope. It finds what hangs from the global object (outside) and what it is handed (handed), and may call both with anything.
# It finds no variable of a module and no object that only such a variable leads to: `hidden.run()` has one callee, and nobody but that call enters `inside`.
# It cannot replace Array.prototype.map, which compiled code relies on: the call of map has one callee
